# CR 702.16, 113.7a, 608.2h: a permanent's protection from a player is from the sources that player controls, and a source that
# has left the battlefield is judged by its controller as it last existed there. Bot2's True-Name Nemesis has protection from
# Bot1 (the chosen player). On turn 4 Bot2 steals Bot1's Fanatical Firebrand with Act of Treason, targets its own Nemesis with
# the Firebrand (legal: Bot2 controls the Firebrand), and sacrifices it as the cost. As the ability resolves the Firebrand is in
# Bot1's graveyard, but its last controller was Bot2, so the target is still legal, nothing prevents the damage, and the 1/1
# Nemesis dies. Judged by its owner Bot1, the Nemesis would be protected and survive.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Fanatical Firebrand
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
True-Name Nemesis
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Act of Treason
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Fanatical Firebrand.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot2.Hand.True-Name Nemesis.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.ChoosePlayer(Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Act of Treason.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Fanatical Firebrand)
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Fanatical Firebrand.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.True-Name Nemesis)
Bot2.Choose(Tap Fanatical Firebrand)
? Bot1.Graveyard = Fanatical Firebrand
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = True-Name Nemesis; Act of Treason; Black Lotus
Bot1.Graveyard = Fanatical Firebrand
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 20
Stack.Count = 0
